# Third-party model weights downloaded for comparison rows, 1.6 GB and re-fetchable.
# `results/external/socratic-qmsum/` is Salesforce's released Socratic SegEnc checkpoint,
# fetched from the Hub. Committing it would bloat the history permanently (git cannot
# easily shed a 1.6 GB blob) and would redistribute someone else's weights from this repo.
# Re-fetch rather than commit. The predictions we generated FROM it are tracked, in
# results/preds/, because those are the paper's releasable artifact.
results/external/

# GGUF export of the promoted adapter (22 MB). Regenerable deterministically from the
# released adapter via llama.cpp convert_lora_to_gguf.py; its SHA256
# (5cf1ee8f659e39a63860d31b2546153fdad624fecd2718e38d532088bf9655e5) pins the artifact
# without committing the binary. Same philosophy as checkpoints/ above.
results/export/
